### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example of a “card” that flips (rotates) around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Holds the card and gives perspective so the 3D effect looks natural */
.card-container {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 1000px;          /* depth of the 3D space */
    margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The actual card element that will rotate */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- Front & Back ----------
   Both sides occupy the same space; back is rotated 180° initially */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside when facing away */
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #fff;
}

.card .front {
    background: #3498db;           /* front side colour */
}

.card .back {
    background: #e74c3c;           /* back side colour */
    transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* start rotated */
}

/* ---------- Hover Effect ----------
   When hovering over the container, rotate the card 180° */
.card-container:hover .card {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-container">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="front">
            Front Side
        </div>
        <div class="back">
            Back Side
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-container` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective: 1000px`). |
| `.card` | Holds the two sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps children in 3D. |
| `.front`, `.back` | The two faces of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away. |
| Hover rule | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

You can replace the colors, text, or add more styling (e.g., images, icons) as needed. Enjoy your rotating card!
